{"title":"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By adding the same constant to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9e8985a89f4776ca097d3c8627abaaea144780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20,50,100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> a geometric progression results. The common ratio is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618854b5895401b71e60155035c8c0769a65a0ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac53 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac43\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac32\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac12\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"367\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the constant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262c5b3c8b76dac7c8d2c3a9e9714891ab6c2942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+x, 50+x, 100+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"177\" height=\"16\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_progression\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric progression\">geometric progression</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b24e26095f1a092bb8d93df892e3768ef647616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20+x)(100+x) = (50+x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"19\" />. Expanding, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800f6447467a169f5ac764a57a0b61244cf0a945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000 + 120x + x^2 = 2500 + 100x + x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"295\" height=\"16\" />; therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/0/f10de2702d44aa07f3d1781c1225b96715ac9071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20x = 500$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08f7cfaaaac737ada39fc1450e9a5319e01a9038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=25$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Now we can calculate our geometric progression to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/263654aa576938a9651cd9e5626b2e3e1fcf6c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20+25, 50+25, 100+25 = 45, 75, 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"304\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, the common ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5958852a17b87c4494e3d3b9462dccdbb6c700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{125}{75} = \\frac{75}{45} = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"126\" height=\"48\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME\" title=\"1959 AHSME\">1959 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1959 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1959\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1959_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1959 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/w